e 34%, clock 34% (median move 29)."],"plan":"Usually continues d4 (34%), Nf3 (28%), Nc3 (9%). Your pawn is the one to watch (often landing on b5, c5). Aim at their pawn.","tips":["Aim for a steady edge by move 13: 53% of games get there, and 40% reach +6 by move 22.","Watch your rook: it is behind 20% of your lost leads, 1.2\u00d7 the usual rate, most often the king's rook (64%), landing on e8, h7, d8.","Aim at their pawn: it is behind 26% of their lost leads, 1.2\u00d7 the usual rate. The reply wins it outright 17% of the time. Take it with a pawn.","Material changes hands for you on d4 and d1: build pressure there.","They win material on c6 and h6: keep those squares defended.","Look for the removing the defender: it appears 3.6\u00d7 as often as usual in this opening."],"similar":[],"family":"Goldsmith Defense","children":[]}